Here is a list of requirements for a set of tokens used for this application:
1. Each token = one beat.
2. The value of a beat is one quarter note.
3. There can be no more than 4 subdivisions of the beat in a token. (4 16th notes)
4. The range of note values is from C3 (middle c) to G4.
5. The notes must be either chord tones or known non-chord tones that correspond to known baroque convention (escape tones, leading tones, etc.)
6. There are four families of tonality: C major, F major, G major, D minor.  
7. Token list: 0 = Quarter Rest, 1-3= quarter note, 4-6 = pair of eighths, 7-8= four sixteeths, 9= 3:2
8. Duplicates are required to increase or decrease the token pool to a statistically useful pool.  Start with 4 copies of each token.

Instructions:
Theorize this as a card game that is Apples to Apples meets Uno, based on music. 2-4 players

Goal: Players build hands of tokens (beats) to create a phrase that is 4 to 8 beats long.
There is a flop of some amount (say 4 cards) that are house cards.  Any player can use them in their phrase.
Once players have an adqueate hand, they show their hand and play it on their instrument (or sing it). 
Players vote on the best one, then play continues.  Player with the most number of winning phrases wins.

